New Dawn READ ME

In order for the New Dawn (ND) Scripts to function as intended you will need a set of Cargo Boxes:

'CargoIn' This can be an array, as the scripts refer to CargoIn*, so you may have CargoIn1, CargoIn2, CargoInWhatever etc.
'FurnaceIn'
'DeconstrutorIn'
'MountedWeapons'
'MountedWeaponAmmo'
'Misc'
'Meds'
'Fuel'


A storage array of boxes with the prefix 'ST-'. I use ST-1, through to ST-20.

The Script SortingMain-ND will pull all construction materials out of this box 
(i.e. ingots, components (both vanilla and RE) into the storage array.

The Script SortingFurnace-Decon-ND will pull all items that should be broken down, into 2 boxes.
Anything that can be run through the furnace, will put inserted into a box called 'FurnaceIn'.
Attach your Furnace input to this box.
The Furnace Output should be attached to CargoIn.

Anything that can be run through the deconstructor, will be inserted into a box called 'DeconstructorIn'
Attach the deconstructor input to this box. The deconstructor output should be attached to CargoIn.

Note that I'm also putting Titanium Plates and Sathium plates into the Furnace.
These will turn back into Titanium Ore and Sathium Ore. These are then put back into CargoIn.
Where they are pulled back into the Furnace again, to turn into Ingots.
This is because 1 ore = 2 ingots = 4 plates, and so to reduce space consumption, they are dropped back to ingots.


